Subject: [PATCH 06898/11362] [outer-loop] dc22: round 6 no progress, session
 lost to tooling churn

Round-6 gpt-5.6-sol session confirmed the banked L5 prefix and
re-scouted the same L6 starting state already documented by round 5
(no new information), then spent nearly all its remaining wall-clock
rewriting its own scratch REPL driver script rather than driving
exploration actions. Killed by the 40-minute wall-clock timeout (exit
124) before reaching a stopping point or writing a result artifact --
no candidate action sequence was recoverable, unlike the sibling lf52
round-6 session which had saved its state via a REPL 'save' command.
No new level banked; frontier stays at level 5 (matches registry,
no regression). Logged for round-tracking so a future attempt doesn't
repeat the same L6 scouting or unbounded tooling iteration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
